<article class="env-lemma" id="0AZD">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AZD">Lemma <span data-tag="0AZD">43.6.1</span>.</a> Suppose that $f : X \to Y$ is a proper morphism of varieties. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent sheaf with $\dim (\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F})) \leq k$, then $f_*[\mathcal{F}]_ k = [f_*\mathcal{F}]_ k$. In particular, if $Z \subset X$ is a closed subscheme of dimension $\leq k$, then $f_*[Z]_ k = [f_*\mathcal{O}_ Z]_ k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See Chow Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02R6" data-tag="02R6">42.12.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>